    "result_text": "Full suite passes: **275 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the per-city capacity rule: creating an owner is now rejected with **400 Bad Request** when the owner's city already contains 8 owners.\n\nFollowing the existing OfficeFloor function-injection pattern (mirroring the daily-limit rule), I added:\n\n1. **`CheckCityCapacity.java`** \u2014 a pipeline step that counts existing owners in the same city (comparing via `DuplicateKey.normalize`, so casing/whitespace differences are ignored, consistent with `NormaliseCity`) and throws `CityCapacityException` when the count is already \u2265 8 (`CITY_LIMIT`).\n2. **`CityCapacityException.java`** \u2014 a checked exception.\n3. **`CityCapacityExceptionHandler.java`** + escalation YAML \u2014 responds 400 with a `ProblemDetail` body, matching the other 400 handlers.\n4. Wired `checkCityCapacity` into `owners.POST.yml` (under `transaction` governance) between the duplicate-email check and membership-number assignment.\n\nThe pre-existing `Cp14Tests` (which was already present, expecting this behavior) now passes, along with `Cp13Tests` and the rest of the suite.",
